# Example environment file for the telnyx-fde support assistant.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values, then run `npm run deploy`.
# `.env` itself is gitignored and never committed.
#
# TELNYX_API_KEY is required by scripts/deploy.ts to call the Telnyx REST API
# (KV namespace lookup/create, key seed, public-key fetch). Get one from the
# Telnyx Portal -> API Keys -> "Edit / View" -> "API Key". The CLI's own auth
# (telnyx-edge auth status) is separate and not affected by this value.
TELNYX_API_KEY=

# TELNYX_FDE_ADMIN_SECRET protects POST /admin/seed (demo fixtures) and
# GET /admin/check-config (deployment diagnostic). If left empty, the deploy
# script generates a random 32-byte base64 value, appends it to .env, and
# pushes it to Telnyx as a secret. If you prefer to set your own, fill it here
# before the first run; the script will then push that value to Telnyx.
TELNYX_FDE_ADMIN_SECRET=
